B. Learning, constructivist, and information processing: This approach emphasizes the role of learning and the construction of knowledge in development, and the ways in which individuals process and interpret information to understand the world around them.

C. Biological, evolutionary, and cognitive: This approach integrates biological and evolutionary perspectives with cognitive theories of development, highlighting the role of genetics and evolution in shaping cognitive abilities and behaviors.
